  "answer_text": "Here is a summary of the latest news on **Ukraine** (as of May 31, 2026):\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\uddfa\ud83c\udde6 Ukraine \u2014 Latest News\n\n### \u2694\ufe0f Military Situation\n\n- Russia's advance has suddenly stalled, and Ukraine is fighting on its own terms \u2014 a comeback credited to Kyiv's efforts to steadily strengthen the capabilities of its UAVs (drones).\n\n- Ukrainian Commander-in-Chief Oleksandr Syrskii stated that Ukraine has seized the tactical initiative, as Ukrainian offensive assaults on Russian positions now outnumber Russian assaults on Ukrainian positions.\n\n- General Oleksandr Komarenko of the Ukrainian General Staff claimed that Ukrainian forces had restored control over 285.6 km\u00b2 in the Oleksandrivka direction. In total, Ukrainian forces cleared 400 km\u00b2 of territory since the beginning of counteroffensive operations, and February 2026 was the first month since 2024 when Ukraine regained more territory than it lost.\n\n- Ukraine is making a fresh offensive push on the southern front, and according to the May 29 update of Deep State's map, the village of Novoselivka in Dnipropetrovsk Oblast has been liberated from Russian occupation.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\ude81 Drone Warfare\n\n- Ukraine has scaled up attacks on refineries across Russia in 2026. Ukrainian drone attacks knocked out about 700,000 barrels per day of refining capacity between January and May across 16 refineries \u2014 compared with eight refineries in the same period of 2025.\n\n- The Ukrainian military destroyed two Russian Tu-142 naval aircraft and an Iskander missile system at a military airfield in Taganrog, Rostov Oblast.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca3 Russian Attacks & Casualties\n\n- According to the UN human rights office (OHCHR), more civilians were killed or injured in Ukraine during the first four months of 2026 than during the same period in 2025, with 815 civilian deaths and 4,174 injuries verified between January and April.\n\n- Russian attacks killed 5 and injured 40 across Ukraine over one recent day, also destroying a train station in Sumy Oblast.\n\n- According to Ukraine's General Staff, Russia has lost an estimated 1,362,500 troops in Ukraine since February 24, 2022, including 1,430 casualties in just one recent day.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf0d International Response\n\n- The United Nations warned of a dangerous escalation in the war after large-scale Russian strikes, with Secretary-General Ant\u00f3nio Guterres saying the conflict risks spiralling \"out of control\" due to the dangers of miscalculation and \"unknown and unintended consequences.\"\n\n- NATO condemned a \"reckless\" Russian drone strike on a Romanian apartment building.\n\n- Japan bought over $14 million in military equipment for Ukraine under a NATO weapons program, though Japan's contribution is limited to non-lethal aid.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f Political Developments\n\n- Kyrylo Budanov, head of Ukrainian military intelligence (HUR), was appointed to replace Andriy Yermak as head of the Office of the President of Ukraine.\n\n- President Zelensky met top officials and announced preparations for \"important negotiations,\" with top agenda items including Ukraine's urgent need to acquire more air defense interceptor missiles and joint drone production agreements with the US and European partners.\n\n---\n\nThe situation in Ukraine remains extremely active, with intense fighting, drone warfare, and ongoing diplomatic efforts. Would you like more detail on any specific aspect?",
